// A KEY change that lands at a line break — the END-OF-LINE COURTESY GROUP.
//
// LilyPond prints a changed signature on BOTH sides of a break: the real one in the new
// system's prefix, and a COURTESY at the end of the line before it. KeySignature's
// break-visibility is all-visible (scm/define-grobs.scm:1979 begin-of-line-visible for the
// cancellation, and the key engraver's explicitKeySignatureVisibility for the signature), so
// what stands at the old line's end is: cancellation, then the new key, then the new meter if
// that changed too.
//
// ⚠️ WHY THIS FIXTURE EXISTS. Until 2026-08-03 NO fixture changed key across a break, so the
// whole end-of-line courtesy KEY path had no snapshot at all — only one ledger point
// (courtesy.meter.barline-to-cancellation) watched it. That was found the hard way: moving
// SpacingRules.BarlineToCourtesyKey from an invented 0.8 to LilyPond's declared 1.0 changed
// the drawing and not one snapshot moved. test/timesig-change-linebreak covers the METER side
// of the same group; this covers the key, and the second break covers both together.
//
// The three gaps this pins, all of them BarLine's or the left grob's own space-alist entry
// (lily/break-alignment-interface.cc:180-210 keys the LEFT grob's alist by the RIGHT grob's
// break-align-symbol, and :241-243 makes the ink-to-ink gap exactly that entry):
//   bar → cancellation   1.00   BarLine         (key-cancellation . (extra-space . 1.0))  :297
//   cancellation → key   0.50   KeyCancellation (key-signature    . (extra-space . 0.5))  :1944
//   key → meter          1.15   KeySignature    (time-signature   . (extra-space . 1.15)) :1989
//
// ⚠️ THE BREAKS ARE EXPLICIT, not left to the line breaker. A fixture that relied on wide
// measures to fall in the right place would stop testing this the day a spacing constant
// moved, and would do it silently.
//
// ✔ VERIFIED TO GUARD, not assumed to: putting BarlineToCourtesyKey back to 0.8 fails THIS
// snapshot and no other (200 pass, 1 fails). A fixture that does not move when the constant
// moves is the very hole this one fills, so the check is part of adding it.

title "Key Change at Line Break"
composer "Lily#"

time 4/4
key ees major

part melody { clef treble }

section Main {
  melody {
    // Line 1 ends with a courtesy CANCELLATION + the new key: three flats go, three sharps come.
    g4 a b a |
    break
    key a major
    // Line 2 ends with cancellation, key AND meter — the shape a real book has, and the only
    // one that puts the 1.15 key→meter gap at a line END rather than in a system prefix.
    b4 a g a |
    break
    key f major
    time 3/4
    a4 g f |
  }
}

form main { Main }

score main "key-change-linebreak" {
  staff melody
}
